  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "For the universal set $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU={5,10,15,20,25,30,35},\n$$\n\nfind the truth set of $P(x)\u21d2Q(x)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer.",
  "worked_solution": "Since $P(x)\u21d2Q(x)\u2261\u00acP(x)\u2228Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={T}_{\u00acP\u2228Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{\u00acP}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={5,15,25,35}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the complement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{5,15,25,35}} \\\\  & ={10,20,30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={25}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u21d2Q} & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={10,20,30}\\cup {25} \\\\  & ={10,20,25,30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
